    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >About 1,000 years ago, Bargon of Ias, a mere mercenary in the land of Ias, accidentally obtained the magical ring Galtea, which was created by the great mage Oudius and emits vast amounts of energy, and gained great power. With his power, Bargon misused the ring to commit misdeeds in the cities of the world, slaughtering many citizens and invading many countries. He lived in the labyrinth of Apollonios, where he practiced daily, and his power grew even more powerful. Bargon is now studying magic day and night to rule the world and further amplify his evil power. King Propertius of Diaga, the ruler of the largest country on the frontier, has placed a bounty of 30,000,000 gold on the heads of brave men and women from all over the world who can defeat Bargon and retrieve the ring.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a Dungeon RPG in which the objective is to defeat the Demon King Bargon in a huge dungeon that stretches across 18 underground floors and retrieve Galtea's ring. Movement is progression-based, but battles are turn-based.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The player will talk to NPCs in the dungeon to improve his or her knowledge of the dungeon and how to conquer it. You can get gold and items by defeating monsters. You can also get items by opening treasure chests hidden in the dungeon. There is a store in the dungeon where you can buy items. There are gimmicks such as elevators that allow you to go up and down floors, revolving doors, stairs, teleporters that allow you to move instantly, balls that allow you to move, and a very narrow single-story bridge. These gimmicks and traps are to be exploited to find the Bargon that lurks in this dungeon.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >About 1,000 years ago, Bargon of Ias, a mere mercenary in the land of Ias, accidentally obtained the magical ring Galtea, which was created by the great mage Oudius and emits vast amounts of energy, and gained great power. With his power, Bargon misused the ring to commit misdeeds in the cities of the world, slaughtering many citizens and invading many countries. He lived in the labyrinth of Apollonios, where he practiced daily, and his power grew even more powerful. Bargon is now studying magic day and night to rule the world and further amplify his evil power. King Propertius of Diaga, the ruler of the largest country on the frontier, has placed a bounty of 30,000,000 gold on the heads of brave men and women from all over the world who can defeat Bargon and retrieve the ring.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a Dungeon RPG in which the objective is to defeat the Demon King Bargon in a huge dungeon that stretches across 18 underground floors and retrieve Galtea's ring. Movement is progression-based, but battles are turn-based.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The player will talk to NPCs in the dungeon to improve his or her knowledge of the dungeon and how to conquer it. You can get gold and items by defeating monsters. You can also get items by opening treasure chests hidden in the dungeon. There is a store in the dungeon where you can buy items. There are gimmicks such as elevators that allow you to go up and down floors, revolving doors, stairs, teleporters that allow you to move instantly, balls that allow you to move, and a very narrow single-story bridge. These gimmicks and traps are to be exploited to find the Bargon that lurks in this dungeon.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "short_description": "This is a Dungeon RPG where players form a party of up to seven people and search for and defeat the Demon King Balgon in a huge dungeon that stretches 18 floors underground, and reclaim Galtea's ring. Movement is in real time, but combat is turn-based.",
